  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the larger variance. Variance can be computed from the outcomes and probabilities. For Lottery A: outcomes are 4000 (20%) and 0 (80%). The expected value is (0.2 × 4000) + (0.8 × 0) = 800. Variance = 0.2 × (4000 - 800)^2 + 0.8 × (0 - 800)^2 = 0.2 × (3200)^2 + 0.8 × (800)^2 = 0.2 × 10,240,000 + 0.8 × 640,000 = 2,048,000 + 512,000 = 2,560,000. For Lottery B: outcomes are 3000 (25%) and 0 (75%). Expected value = (0.25 × 3000) + (0.75 × 0) = 750. Variance = 0.25 × (3000 - 750)^2 + 0.75 × (0 - 750)^2 = 0.25 × (2250)^2 + 0.75 × (750)^2 = 0.25 × 5,062,500 + 0.75 × 562,500 = 1,265,625 + 421,875 = 1,687,500. Thus, Lottery A has a higher variance (2,560,000 > 1,687,500), so the decision reason would prefer Lottery A.",
